.TH RECALLCTL 1 "2026-03-23" "systemd-recalld 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
recallctl \- control the systemd-recalld capture daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B recallctl
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B recallctl
is the command-line interface for controlling the
.BR systemd-recalld (8)
desktop audio and video capture daemon. It communicates with the daemon
via D-Bus.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the current capture status, including whether capture is active,
the number of stored captures, and total storage used.
.TP
.B start
Start capturing audio and video from the desktop.
.TP
.B stop
Stop all active captures.
.TP
.B pause
Temporarily pause capturing without stopping the daemon.
.TP
.B resume
Resume capturing after a pause.
.TP
.BI list " [TYPE]"
List stored captures. TYPE can be
.BR audio ", " video ", or " screenshot .
Defaults to
.BR audio .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (connection error, invalid command, etc.)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Check if capture is running
recallctl status

# Start capture
recallctl start

# Pause and resume
recallctl pause
recallctl resume

# List recent audio captures
recallctl list audio
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-recalld (8),
.BR systemd-recall-query-service (8)
